explanation:
{
    "explanation": "Q1 computes the fraction of groups where the minimum date has a consecutive date in the same group, while Q2 computes the fraction of groups that have any consecutive dates starting from the minimum date. The key difference is that Q1 checks only if (min_date + 1) exists for each group, whereas Q2 checks if there exists any consecutive pair (A1.c2 + 1 = A2.c2) where A1.c2 is the minimum date for that group. Q2's condition (A1.c4, A1.c2) IN (SELECT c4, MIN(c2) FROM table1 GROUP BY c4) ensures A1.c2 is the minimum date, but it doesn't require A2.c2 to be exactly (min_date + 1) - it could be any date that's one day after A1.c2, which might not be the immediate next date after the minimum if there are gaps.",
